# TeamStarWolf reference library — ignore IDE/OS/secret artifacts only.
# This is a static docsify site (no build step); NOTHING that is served
# (*.md, data/**, navigator/**, mitre/**, index.html, _*.md, assets/**) is ignored.
# Added to prevent recurrence of the .vs/ PII class (audit F-lylat-and-prior-9).

# Visual Studio / VS "hidden" state (this is the .vs/ leak class)
.vs/
*.vsidx
*.suo
*.wsuo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates
slnx.sqlite
# Copilot / editor local index DBs
**/CodeChunks.db
**/SemanticSymbols.db

# VS Code (ignore local state; keep any intentionally shared settings out of the repo)
.vscode/

# JetBrains
.idea/
*.iml

# Claude / agent local state
.claude/

# Node (in case tooling is ever added)
node_modules/
/coverage/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Secrets / env — never commit real values (examples like *.env.example stay tracked).
# NOTE: deliberately NOT using *secret*/*credential*/*password*/*token* filename globs —
# this library legitimately ships reference docs named e.g. PASSWORD_SECURITY_REFERENCE.md,
# and those globs would silently exclude real content. Ignore by extension/exact env only.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12

# Local databases / dumps
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
